# Sitting r0928, job `join` (item 4; ideaaudit-card-report.md §0 row 7 line 33, from
# v41-audit-gpu-report.md:90-93 and plan-ledger:1018 / :1159). The card report puts the join's fixed
# cost at 36 us a layer (40 layers, 1.44 ms of the 22.3 ms hot-list step, 6.5 %); that 36.0 is the
# intercept of kr-moeattn's bridge fit 36.0 + 119.5 k_host us, which holds the host's fixed work
# inside the leg (list build, the x copy out of the page, the pool dispatch) as well as the protocol.
# ds41join-predict.txt (wave-m4) split it: leg(k) = 375-385 / 735-745 us at k = 3 / 6, so the bridge
# minus the leg is 10..20 us a service, constant in k: the go batch's two system barriers and the
# generation word crossing PCIe (~2-5), the wait memop polling the counter (~2-5), the post kernel's
# launch after the wait (~3-5) [derived]. That split is the term here; the two reports do not
# disagree, they name different spans. The host report's (b) 21-36 us floor is the same intercept.
# Minutes: 4 [derived: the V4.1 load 75-117 s (rig-log 09-26 nsyspp: 74.6 s; r8host-pp: 33 min for
# 16 loads), 8 decode steps, the nsys export].
kind: profile
question: how much of a V4.1 host join is protocol (signals, polls, the post launch) and not host
  compute, with the hot list on?
term: (the mean host bridge a replay, go to join over all layers, from nsys) minus (the mean leg_us a
  step, stat step) over (the mean served a step), V4.1 plan (a), hot list 384, lcg depth 6, n = 8,
  A6000
unit: us
predict: 10..20
condition: BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_HOT_LIST=/root/bloomery-data/router/hotlist-384.txt
  BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/r0928-join-nsys.card' just nsys-gpu-ds41 6
  under the lease on the A6000: the runner's bridge line (host bridge, all layers, a replay mean over
  the tabled replays) and the run log's stat step lines of the same steps (the kept, non-warm ones);
  the runner's replay-count check passes or no table; the step's served count must be the plan's
  routed layers every step (a step serving fewer is void); guard_other records the 3090
decide-in: the protocol is 0.4..0.8 ms a step (2-4 %): the join-floor levers (the layer word in the
  image, the post spinning on the counter, BAR1 writes; kr-moeattn J2) are worth at most half that,
  under a round's worth: record them as held behind adaptive residency in the idea ledger
decide-below: the protocol is under 0.4 ms a step: the join floor is host work inside the leg, not
  signalling; reject the protocol levers and price the leg's fixed part (list build, x copy, the
  pool dispatch) with the next host round instead
decide-above: the protocol is past 0.8 ms a step: open a join-protocol design round (S-M) on
  kr-moeattn's (a)-(c) with its own A/B card, the lever predicted from this row
